it is a big day for the clark county  school district later tonight the board  will vote on a plan  to possibly allow students back on  campus many parents and teachers though  have mixed opinions on this proposal  bianca holman is live from the school  board office  with more on this hi bianca hey good  morning alex  the school board actually posted a 205  page document and that's the  transitional plan and it's a hybrid  model to get kids back into the  classroom and  as you can expect of course parents and  teachers there's a  range of opinions regarding that  transitional plan now here's a little  bit more about what was included  the proposed plan includes two days of  face-to-face learning and three days of  distance learning for students each week  some students will be back in the  classroom as soon as january 4th  however parents will have the option to  remain in full-time distance learning if  they choose  strict cleaning protocols and  transportation requirements are included  in the plan as well  the school district posted a  questionnaire for cohort cohort  selections  this is information they would use to  implement the plan  we spoke with rebecca garcia the nevada  pta president  she says many parents are relieved to  finally have a plan in part for in the  in-person instruction  but there's still major concerns  one of the things that i hope i see the  trustees focus  on very specifically is the quality of  distance learning  because even in the hybrid model  students are still going to be spending  three out of five days a week in  distance education  and we know that at least a decent  percentage  maybe even up to half or more will  continue full-time  in distance education  and so if you're a parent and you have  not viewed the plan or completed the  survey you can do so by visiting the  district website  click on the plan transitional picture  it's right on that main landing page  when you go to it  and so again the board of trustees  they're meeting later on today at 5 pm  to discuss that hybrid transitional  model  again looking to implement that come at  the top of the january the top of the  year  reporting live from ccsd headquarters  bianca holman  8 news now
 

